{
    "background_story": "Shay was a skilled but reckless stunt driver who made a name for himself in the underground racing scene. He was known for taking on the most treacherous courses, earning him the nickname 'Deathtrap' among his peers. Shay's vehicle of choice was a heavily modified muscle car, which he had outfitted with nitrous oxide and a roll cage. One fateful night, Shay took on the infamous 'Devil's Gauntlet' - a notorious stretch of abandoned highway notorious for its sharp turns and steep cliffs. As he pushed his car to the limit, Shay's luck finally ran out. His vehicle skidded off the road, and he narrowly escaped with his life. The incident served as a wake-up call, and Shay eventually retired from racing, opening a driving school to teach others the importance of safety and caution behind the wheel.",
